      "seed": 509145978,
      "version": 48,
      "versionNonce": 453308713,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1779023241499,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Client",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "vJF16y77EUUSg7EwuFNnI",
      "originalText": "Client",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "yh2Wdy5MmpmBTBfe7VwOH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 477.9048418317522,
      "y": 2391.5000871930847,
      "width": 1233.1790771484375,
      "height": 1025,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2S",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 474785018,
      "version": 1922,
      "versionNonce": 953995751,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1779023241499,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Solution to all above problem with design\n1) Consistency = Double booking (same seat booked two times)\nSolution 1) : we can introduce new column bookingTime \n -> if user still not done payment and other user search for show and if time elapsed (10min) reserved seat will be \navailabe to user \nproblem with solution 1:\n-> query became complex\n-> If User or service was down this status won't change it has still same booking status \n    Solution for this use cron job to change each seat status after 1hr interval ( assume)\nbut again it has same problem if seat booked just after corn job run then it will have booking status for 59 min.\n\n\nREDIS LOCK\nTo resolve it we use redis lock with TTL\nTTL = 10 min \nbook seat = client -> booking service -> validate seat and do locking on it by put entry in redis\npayment of book seat = client -> booking service -> stripe -> booking service -> remove entry from redis ->\nchange status of seat to booking in db \nFailed payment of book seat => redis still have entry which will be removed after 10 min.\n\n\n\n2) Latency = Search service query DB for shows/events/seat etc\nSolution:1 \nUsed Elastic search when do search\nElastic search do perform better here because it has invarted index which help user to search using like in document file.\n\nUsed redis for getting event data\nRedis used as cache between event service and db so minium db call happend which can improve latency as well as performance.\n\n3) Availability = DB can be single point of failure\nSolution : 1\nWe will do replication logic over here so we can reduce spof.\nHere mainly concern is ticket table data as other data are static which is update very min.\n\n4) Scalability = Search can be overloaded due to milion user query DB for show ( celebrity problem)\nSolution:1 \nUsed Elastic search when do search\nElastic search do perform better here because it has invarted index which help user to search using like in document file.\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Solution to all above problem with design\n1) Consistency = Double booking (same seat booked two times)\nSolution 1) : we can introduce new column bookingTime \n -> if user still not done payment and other user search for show and if time elapsed (10min) reserved seat will be \navailabe to user \nproblem with solution 1:\n-> query became complex\n-> If User or service was down this status won't change it has still same booking status \n    Solution for this use cron job to change each seat status after 1hr interval ( assume)\nbut again it has same problem if seat booked just after corn job run then it will have booking status for 59 min.\n\n\nREDIS LOCK\nTo resolve it we use redis lock with TTL\nTTL = 10 min \nbook seat = client -> booking service -> validate seat and do locking on it by put entry in redis\npayment of book seat = client -> booking service -> stripe -> booking service -> remove entry from redis ->\nchange status of seat to booking in db \nFailed payment of book seat => redis still have entry which will be removed after 10 min.\n\n\n\n2) Latency = Search service query DB for shows/events/seat etc\nSolution:1 \nUsed Elastic search when do search\nElastic search do perform better here because it has invarted index which help user to search using like in document file.\n\nUsed redis for getting event data\nRedis used as cache between event service and db so minium db call happend which can improve latency as well as performance.\n\n3) Availability = DB can be single point of failure\nSolution : 1\nWe will do replication logic over here so we can reduce spof.\nHere mainly concern is ticket table data as other data are static which is update very min.\n\n4) Scalability = Search can be overloaded due to milion user query DB for show ( celebrity problem)\nSolution:1 \nUsed Elastic search when do search\nElastic search do perform better here because it has invarted index which help user to search using like in document file.\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "x5oezkHZtLmAs769O_0dw",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1833.9762704031807,
      "y": 2456.5000871930843,
      "width": 705.199462890625,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2U",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1202533498,
      "version": 396,
      "versionNonce": 1837032457,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1779023241499,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Elastic search (Data update)\n1) Long pooling which will pool data from db and update in elastic search\n -> problem => IO call which time consuming\n\n2) Cron job \n-> problem => fixed interval due to which possibility of update miss.\n\n3) CDC \n-> real time update reflected in Elastic search",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Elastic search (Data update)\n1) Long pooling which will pool data from db and update in elastic search\n -> problem => IO call which time consuming\n\n2) Cron job \n-> problem => fixed interval due to which possibility of update miss.\n\n3) CDC \n-> real time update reflected in Elastic search",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
