    {
      "id": "dO0Nmo_NfaKUj-9OylrFn",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1851.1191275460378,
      "y": 2720.071515764513,
      "width": 673.839599609375,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2X",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1935786662,
      "version": 482,
      "versionNonce": 327205927,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1779023241499,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Redis cache\n1) write through cache \n-> consistent and update are very minimum almost 1 out of 100\n\nWhy Redis: in memory-database which is faster compared to DB \nwell performed in distributed env and it is single threaded application\n\n\nRedis lock\n-> What data will need to store => userId: | seat: | ttl:\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Redis cache\n1) write through cache \n-> consistent and update are very minimum almost 1 out of 100\n\nWhy Redis: in memory-database which is faster compared to DB \nwell performed in distributed env and it is single threaded application\n\n\nRedis lock\n-> What data will need to store => userId: | seat: | ttl:\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "u7gLEiU-Kr9LRWtm2UBds",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 485.0476989746094,
      "y": 3435.785801478798,
      "width": 1286.618896484375,
      "height": 700,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2Y",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1770257978,
      "version": 1529,
      "versionNonce": 1962554825,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1779023241499,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Main Problem\nCelebrity problem\n1) How we can handle celebrity problem\n-> Over here we need to separate out popular event based on hashing because locking , db query , elastic serarch all will impacted.\n-> but db and elastic are that much capable to handle load\n-> For booking we need some improvement booking service got bumbarded -> lets put queue and ask user you are in queue for 10 min\nand when got successfully reserved asked user for payment with notification.\n\n\nAchieved both functional and non-functional\n\nOther problems\nNow seat will be fixed if you update same table which is problem.\nNeed to create physical seats and logical seats\nphysical seat stored as blueprint and logical seats are used for status updated.\n\nUse CDN \nWhich can store and return search reponse. \nproblem :- cost and search query can be change suppose 1M request all have different parameter then all store in CDN cause issue.\n\nSharding \n-> celebrity problem \n-> region based \npros: improve performance as request got distributed among the instance\ncons: maintains, failure replacement etc..\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Main Problem\nCelebrity problem\n1) How we can handle celebrity problem\n-> Over here we need to separate out popular event based on hashing because locking , db query , elastic serarch all will impacted.\n-> but db and elastic are that much capable to handle load\n-> For booking we need some improvement booking service got bumbarded -> lets put queue and ask user you are in queue for 10 min\nand when got successfully reserved asked user for payment with notification.\n\n\nAchieved both functional and non-functional\n\nOther problems\nNow seat will be fixed if you update same table which is problem.\nNeed to create physical seats and logical seats\nphysical seat stored as blueprint and logical seats are used for status updated.\n\nUse CDN \nWhich can store and return search reponse. \nproblem :- cost and search query can be change suppose 1M request all have different parameter then all store in CDN cause issue.\n\nSharding \n-> celebrity problem \n-> region based \npros: improve performance as request got distributed among the instance\ncons: maintains, failure replacement etc..\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Dngaj7Ibona-V0rR-vI8B",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1684.8096037365149,
      "y": -99.9284842354889,
      "width": 380.5597839355469,
      "height": 550,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2Z",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 288236407,
      "version": 552,
      "versionNonce": 390309703,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1779023241499,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Missing parts\npotential deep dive\n\n1) Double booking\n-> Optimistic lock (db level)\n-> timeout with table and cron job\n-> timeout with table and read request\n-> Redis lock with TTL\n\n2) Event search\n-> DB index \n-> Mview\n-> Redis cache\n-> Elastic search\n\n3) Celebrity problem\n-> real time seat update (SSE)\n-> virtual waiting queue\n\n4) Frq search query\n-> Using redis or memcached\n-> using caching and edge caching",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Missing parts\npotential deep dive\n\n1) Double booking\n-> Optimistic lock (db level)\n-> timeout with table and cron job\n-> timeout with table and read request\n-> Redis lock with TTL\n\n2) Event search\n-> DB index \n-> Mview\n-> Redis cache\n-> Elastic search\n\n3) Celebrity problem\n-> real time seat update (SSE)\n-> virtual waiting queue\n\n4) Frq search query\n-> Using redis or memcached\n-> using caching and edge caching",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
