    {
      "id": "cDGZ4L8Kj7yFQBmrGxLQh",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1791.0596037365149,
      "y": 1943.8215157645109,
      "width": 1282.619384765625,
      "height": 500,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2l",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 864450080,
      "version": 853,
      "versionNonce": 1581428807,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1779023241499,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Flow\n\n1) Load screen using data (\nsearch data by fixed criteria\nbased on location (city wise))\n\n2) User search using specific cretria\nlike movie, theator name, show timinig\nand price ( keyword)\n\n3) Return search data.\n\nThis will help to put lower load on ES as well as DB.\n\nCAn't used for transactional data (seat) possible seat which is now reserved or unreserved will be reserved or unreserved \njust after user received search data. and also it is not good idea to updated es for each event look for batch update.\n\nEven ES goes down won't impact system, but it will start overhead on DB. so for the overhead and latency we need to introducde\nmaster + replica logic for ES.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Flow\n\n1) Load screen using data (\nsearch data by fixed criteria\nbased on location (city wise))\n\n2) User search using specific cretria\nlike movie, theator name, show timinig\nand price ( keyword)\n\n3) Return search data.\n\nThis will help to put lower load on ES as well as DB.\n\nCAn't used for transactional data (seat) possible seat which is now reserved or unreserved will be reserved or unreserved \njust after user received search data. and also it is not good idea to updated es for each event look for batch update.\n\nEven ES goes down won't impact system, but it will start overhead on DB. so for the overhead and latency we need to introducde\nmaster + replica logic for ES.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
